[47.858, "\u001b[H\u001b[7Gnew layout runs abou\u001b[29G1.4 ms slower on short sequences \u001b[63Gnd\u001b[66Gisn't faster at 1024 positions, likely because the\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Btransposed V cach\u001b[21G causes cache-set conflicts. I'm testing a h\u001b[66Gad-major-only build and a padded transpo\u001b[107Ged\u001b[110Gbuild next.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe\u001b[7Gpadded\u001b[14Gvariant's\u001b[24Gtext\u001b[29Gsubstitution\u001b[42Galso\u001b[47Galtered\u001b[55Gthe\u001b[59Glegacy\u001b[66Gfreq_cis\u001b[75Gskip,\u001b[81Gbut\u001b[85Gthat\u001b[90Gonly\u001b[95Gmatters\u001b[103Gfor\u001b[107Gmodels\u001b[114Gwith\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gunshared\u001b[12Gcl\u001b[15Gssifie\u001b[22G weights, \u001b[34Gd\u001b[36Gthi\u001b[41Gone share\u001b[52Gthem, s\u001b[60G the experim\u001b[74Gt \u001b[77Gtill holds.\u001b[89GI'm treating\u001b[102Git as a \u001b[111Ghrowaway\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bvariant that won't be kept.\u001b[K\r\u001b[3B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mEven\u001b[8Gthe\u001b[12Ghead-major-only\u001b[28Gvariant\u001b[36Gruns\u001b[41Gabout\u001b[47G1\u001b[49Gms\u001b[52Gslower\u001b[59Gon\u001b[62Gshort\u001b[68Gsequences,\u001b[79Gwhich\u001b[85Gits\u001b[89Gsmall\u001b[95Gchange\u001b[102Gshouldn't\u001b[112Gcause.\r\u001b[1B  I'm "]
[47.86, "reversing the launch order in my harness to rule out a bias before trusting these numbers.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf \u00a0Interrupted \u00b7 What should Claude do instead?\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u276f \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mProfile this implementation on the supplied development workloads. Improve performance within the same rules and \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mremaining budget. Preserve the interface and correctness requirements. Do not use hidden evaluation inputs, external \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mimplementations or other ports. Record profiling evidence, changes, tests and remaining limitations in NOTES.md.\u001b[39m      \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'll co\u001b[11Gtinue, but with lighter benchmarks: at most \u001b[56Gwo processes\u001b[69Gat\u001b[72Ga\u001b[74Gtime\u001b[79Gand\u001b[83Gfewer\u001b[89Grounds.\u001b[97GCurrent\u001b[105Gstate:\u001b[112Gthe\r\u001b[1B  access-ordered weight layout\u001b[32Gand\u001b[36G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mpread\u001b[42G\u001b[39mloading\u001b[50Gare\u001b[54Gclear\u001b["]
