[49.318, "slower per forward, and at 1024 positions they were within noise.\u001b[114GI'll\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Brevert the KV cache to the reference layout and keep the\u001b[60Grest.\r\u001b[2B  \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRead \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file, ran \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m The checks pass. Now one bit-exactness comparison with the pre-KV build at 1024 positions,\u001b[94Gthen\u001b[99Ga\u001b[101Gfinal\u001b[107Gtwo-process\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B benchmark of the original build against the final one.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u23fa\u001b[39m Verifying bit-exactness and\u001b[31Gbenchmarking original vs\u001b[56Gfinal\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf  $ python3 /tmp/cbtest/cmp.py \"$PWD\" /tmp/cbtest/v_cur ./cb && uptime && VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1 python3 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m/tmp/cbtest/ab.py \"$PWD\" 8 /tmp/cbtest/v_mmap ./cb\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m\u2736\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;245;149;117mTransmogrifying\u2026\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m(44s \u00b7 \u2193\u001b[29G2.6k tokens)\r\u001b[1B  \u23bf \u00a0Tip: Use /btw to ask a quick side question without interr"]
