[168.469, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BEven\u001b[8Gthe head-major-only variant runs \u001b[42Gbout\u001b[47G1 ms \u001b[53Glower\u001b[59Gon short sequences,\u001b[79Gwhich its\u001b[89Gsmall change shouldn't\u001b[112Gcause.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BI'm reve\u001b[12Gsing th\u001b[20G launch \u001b[29Grder in my harness to \u001b[52Gule out\u001b[60Ga bias b\u001b[69Gfore trusting these \u001b[90Gumbers.\u001b[98G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf \u00a0Interrupted \u00b7 What should Claude do instead?\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u276f \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mProfile this implementation on the supplied development workloads. Improve performance within the same rules and \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mremaining budget. Preserve the interface and correctness requirements. Do not use hidden evaluation inputs, external \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mimplementations or other ports. Record profiling evidence, changes, tests and remaining limitations in NOTES.md.\u001b[39m      \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'll continue, but with\u001b[27Glighter\u001b[35Gbenchmarks:"]
[168.471, "\u001b[47Gat\u001b[50Gmost\u001b[55Gtwo\u001b[59Gprocesses\u001b[69Gat\u001b[72Ga\u001b[74Gtime\u001b[79Gand\u001b[83Gfewer\u001b[89Grounds.\u001b[97GCurrent\u001b[105Gstate:\u001b[112Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Baccess-ordered\u001b[18Gweight\u001b[25Glayout\u001b[32Gand\u001b[36G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mpread\u001b[42G\u001b[39mloading\u001b[50Gare\u001b[54Gclear\u001b[60Gwins.\u001b[66GThe\u001b[70GKV-cache\u001b[79Glayout\u001b[86Gchanges\u001b[94Gare\u001b[98Gnot:\u001b[103Gon\u001b[106Gthe\u001b[110Gshort\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gdevelopment workloads they measured 1\u20131.4 ms slower per forward, and at 1024 pos\u001b[84Gtions they w\u001b[98Ge within\u001b[107Gnoise. I'll\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bver\u001b[9G the\u001b[14GKV cache to the \u001b[31Geference layout \u001b[48Gnd keep\u001b[56Gthe re\u001b[63Gt.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRead \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file, ran \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m The checks pass. Now one bit-exactness comparison with the pre-KV build at 1024 positions, then a final\u001b[107Gtwo-process\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbenchmark of the original build against the final one.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m The final build\u001b[19Gand\u001b[2"]
[168.472, "3Gthe\u001b[27Goriginal\u001b[36Gmmap\u001b[41Gbuild\u001b[47Gnow\u001b[51Gcome\u001b[56Gout\u001b[60Gabout\u001b[66Gequal,\u001b[73Gcontradicting\u001b[87Gthe\u001b[91Gearlier\u001b[99G13.3\u001b[104Gvs\u001b[107G16.5\u001b[112Gms\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B result, so I suspect load or launch-order bias in my harness. I'm running a quick\u001b[85Gcheck:\u001b[92Gthe\u001b[96Gsame\u001b[101Gbinary\u001b[108Gagainst\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B itself, then the pair in reversed order.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u23fa\u001b[39m Reverse-order A/B and sequen\u001b[32Gial workload runs\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf  $ VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1 python3 /tmp/cbtest/ab.py \"$PWD\" 6 ./cb /tmp/cbtest/v_mmap; uptime; \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B \u001b[4G  \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mVECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1 python3 /tmp/cbtest/work.py \"$PWD\" /tmp/cbtest/v_mmap 2; VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1 python3 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m/tmp/cbtest/work.py \"$PWD\" ./cb 2\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m\u2722\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;219;123;91mTransmogrifying\u2026\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m(2m 43s \u00b7 \u2193\u001b[32G3.3k tokens)\r\u001b[1B  \u23bf \u00a0Tip: Use /btw to ask a quick side question without interru"]
