[344.099, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[24C\u001b[33B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m9\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[344.114, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[45C\u001b[33B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mthought for 8s)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[344.166, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[33B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m\u2733\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;245;149;117mT\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;215;119;87mn\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[344.208, "\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 130 \u001b[22m   - FIXED/LOGITS with more than seq_len ids process only the first seq_len.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 131 \u001b[22m   - Out-of-range ids, or an unwritable LOGITS path, answer `ERR ...`.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 132 \u001b[22m   - Unknown commands answer `ERR unknown command`.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 133 \u001b[22m   - Blank lines are ignored.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;207;34;46m\u001b[48;2;255;220;220m  52 -\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Speed:** about 65\u201372 tok/s on this machine for GENERATE with default Accelerate threading.        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI\u001b[5Gimproved weight loading and memory layout. On the supplied workloads the final build is somewhere between equal\u001b[117Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Babout 20% faster per forward pass, but this machine was too busy to pin the number down. It still passes both \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mpython3 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcheck.py\u001b[39m modes, and NOTES.md has the profiling tables, A/B results, tests and limitations.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K"]
[344.21, "\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhere the time goes\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GAbout 98% of each forward pass is in the weight \u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemv\u001b[39m calls. Each one takes time in proportion to its weight bytes\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B(25\u201329 GB/s), so the program is limited by memory bandwidth, not arithmetic.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GAttention is 1.4% on the short fixture sequences and grows to 15% at 1024 positions. Everything else together\u001b[115Gis\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bunder 1%.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GA standalone benchmark of the same BLAS calls puts the floor at about 12\u201313 ms per token. The program runs at\u001b[115Gabout\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B13\u201314.5 ms in quiet periods. Other same-shape BLAS calls (\u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemm\u001b[39m with one column, the transposed \u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemv\u001b[39m forms) and\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BAccelerate's default threading were no faster.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat I changed\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mWeight loading:\u001b[22m weights are now read straight into one aligned buffer, laid out in the order a forward pass uses\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bthem. Before, they were copied out of"]
[344.212, " the file, which stores each matrix type for all layers together. The values\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bare the same: logits over 1024 positions are bit-identical to before.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mProfiling build:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcb.c\u001b[39m has an optional section profiler (\u001b[38;2;87;105;247m-DCB_PROFILE\u001b[39m). It compiles to nothing in the normal build.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mResults\u001b[22m (the machine was shared, load average 3\u201315, so these are noisy)\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GInterleaved comparisons against the original build:\u001b[57G13.29\u001b[63Gvs\u001b[66G16.48\u001b[72Gms,\u001b[76G12.92\u001b[82Gvs\u001b[85G14.22\u001b[91Gms,\u001b[95G16.78\u001b[101Gvs\u001b[104G20.01\u001b[110Gms,\u001b[114Gand\u001b[118Gone\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Btie (14.64 vs 14.40 ms).\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GRun one after the other: 70.2 vs 61.2 forwards/s, and first token in 69 ms instead\u001b[88Gof\u001b[91G89\u001b[94Gms.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GStartup: about 0.9\u20131.5 s with the earlier aligned-copy build,\u001b[67Gnow\u001b[71G0.07\u20130.43\u001b[81Gs.\u001b[84GThe\u001b[88Goriginal\u001b[97Glazy-mapped\u001b[109Gbuild\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Breached READY in 0.03 s but paid that\u001b[43Gcost\u001b[48Glater,\u001b[55Gas\u001b[58"]
[344.212, "Gslow\u001b[63Gfirst\u001b[69Gtokens.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mTried and dropped\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  - Three alternative KV-cache layouts (head-major, and V stored transposed per head). They\u001b[93Gmade\u001b[98Glong-context\u001b[111Gattention\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[344.286, "\u001b]0;\u25d1 Claude Code\u0007"]
[344.657, "\u001b[H\u001b[9G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m3\u001b[16G\u001b[22mBlank lines are ign\u001b[38Gd.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;207;34;46m\u001b[48;2;255;220;220m  52 -\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Speed:** about 65\u201372 tok/s on this machine for GENERATE with default Accelerate threading.        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI\u001b[5Gimproved weight loading and memory layout.\u001b[48GOn\u001b[51Gthe\u001b[55Gsupplied\u001b[64Gworkloads\u001b[74Gthe\u001b[78Gfinal\u001b[84Gbuild\u001b[90Gis\u001b[93Gsomewhere\u001b[103Gbetween\u001b[111Gequal\u001b[117Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Babout 20% faster per forward pass, but this machine was too busy to pin the number down. It still passes both \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mpython3 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcheck.py\u001b[12G\u001b[39mmodes,\u001b[19Gand\u001b[23GNOTES.md\u001b[32Ghas\u001b[36Gthe\u001b[40Gprofiling\u001b[50Gtables,\u001b[58GA/B\u001b[62Gresults,\u001b[71Gtests\u001b[77Gand\u001b[81Glimitations.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhere the time goes\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- About 98% of e\u001b[20Gch\u001b[23Gforward pas\u001b[36Gis in the weight \u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemv\u001b[39m calls. Each\u001b[71Gone takes\u001b[81Gt\u001b[84Ge in proportion\u001b[100Gto\u001b[103Gits\u001b[107Gweight\u001b[114Gbytes\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B(25\u201329\u001b[12GG"]
[344.659, "B/s),\u001b[19Gso\u001b[22Gthe\u001b[26Gprogram\u001b[34Gis\u001b[37Glimited\u001b[45Gby\u001b[48Gmemory\u001b[55Gbandwidth,\u001b[66Gnot\u001b[70Garithmetic.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- Attention is 1.4%\u001b[23Gon\u001b[26Gthe\u001b[30Gshort\u001b[36Gfixture\u001b[44Gsequences\u001b[54Gand\u001b[58Ggrows\u001b[64Gto\u001b[67G15%\u001b[71Gat\u001b[74G1024\u001b[79Gpositions.\u001b[90GEverything\u001b[101Gelse\u001b[106Gtogether\u001b[115Gis\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gunder\u001b[11G1%.\u001b[15G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GA standalone benchmark \u001b[29Gf the \u001b[36Game BLAS\u001b[45Gcalls puts the floor\u001b[66Gat abou\u001b[74G 12\u201313 ms\u001b[84Gper\u001b[88Gtoken.\u001b[95GThe\u001b[99Gprogram\u001b[107Gruns\u001b[112Gat\u001b[115Gabout\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5G13\u201314.5 ms in quiet periods. Other same-shape BLAS calls (\u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemm\u001b[39m with\u001b[74Gone column, the\u001b[90Gtransposed\u001b[101G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247msgemv\u001b[39m forms) and\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BAcc\u001b[9Glerate's\u001b[18Gdefault\u001b[26Gthreading\u001b[36Gwere\u001b[41Gno\u001b[44Gfaster.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat I changed\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mWeight loading:\u001b[22m weigh\u001b[27Gs are \u001b[34Gow read str\u001b[46Gight into\u001b[56Gone\u001b[60Galigned\u001b[68Gbuffer,\u001b[76Glaid\u001b[81Gout\u001b[85Gin\u001b[88Gthe\u001b[92Gorder\u001b[98Ga\u001b[100Gforward\u001b[108Gpass\u001b[113Guse"]
